# mcfish perft gate: FEN|depth|expected-nodes[|variant], pipe-separated, '#' comments.
#
# Deliberately NOT named *.golden: these counts are FACTS about chess, identical
# for every correct engine, so `golden-update` must never touch them. A mismatch
# here is always a movegen bug in mcfish — never a stale expectation.
#
# Between them these positions cover castling on both sides, en-passant including
# the pinned-ep case, under-promotion, double check, and king-safety edge cases.
#
# The fourth field is the variant: `960` drives the row with UCI_Chess960 set, which
# is not optional decoration — the flag reaches Position::set and changes which
# castling legality test runs. Every count below was derived from the PRISTINE oracle
# at tools/upstream/UPSTREAM_BASE, never from mcfish.
rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1|5|4865609
r3k2r/p1ppqpb1/bn2pnp1/3PN3/1p2P3/2N2Q1p/PPPBBPPP/R3K2R w KQkq -|4|4085603
8/2p5/3p4/KP5r/1R3p1k/8/4P1P1/8 w - -|6|11030083
r3k2r/Pppp1ppp/1b3nbN/nP6/BBP1P3/q4N2/Pp1P2PP/R2Q1RK1 w kq -|5|15833292
rnbq1k1r/pp1Pbppp/2p5/8/2B5/8/PPP1NnPP/RNBQK2R w KQ -|4|2103487
r4rk1/1pp1qppp/p1np1n2/2b1p1B1/2B1P1b1/P1NP1N2/1PP1QPPP/R4RK1 w - -|4|3894594
#
# Chess960 castling where the king's destination is on the OPPOSITE side from the
# rook: a king on b1 castling queen-side moves RIGHT, to c1. No standard-chess
# position can reach that shape, so the six rows above are all blind to it. The
# first is the position the weekly differential caught mcfish crashing on; the two
# minimal ones isolate the walk itself — with a1 unattacked (where the bad walk ran
# off the board) and with a1 attacked but c1 free (where it answered the wrong
# question and rejected a legal castling).
1knqbrnb/rp2p1p1/8/N1pp1p1p/6P1/3P3N/PPPBPP1P/RK1Q1R1B w FAf - 0 7|4|1590804|960
1k6/8/8/8/8/8/8/RK6 w A - 0 1|6|341689|960
rk6/8/8/8/8/8/8/RK6 w Aa - 0 1|6|4658743|960
